60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Option A gives me fixed days. I can plan my clinic trips without asking.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,May,,"Option C divides costs by distance. That’s fair, but who records it?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Servas,,Option B puts the burden on one person. That creates the favour-asking trap.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Takumi,,Option A avoids the checking. It’s neutral. I don’t have to ask anyone.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"Option C is fair for fuel, but the admin might be too much.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@May, if I have fixed days, I don’t need to record every run.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,May,,"@Misaki, but what if I need the car on your day? I’d have to ask.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@May, asking is the problem. Option A removes the need to ask for routine use.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Servas, I agree. Option A is the safest for our relationships.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Takumi, but Option A ignores the fuel disparity. Two people drive half.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I vote A. It guarantees my car is ready and mine on my days.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,May,,I vote A. It stops the evening admin. I can plan my weekends.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Servas,,I vote A. It is the most stable and avoids the favour trap.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Takumi,,I vote A. It prevents the resentment of checking figures.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I vote C. I need the fuel costs to be split by actual use.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
